    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d345">

                <pb facs="0337" n="327" xml:id="pg327"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.24/177: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Argentina</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-09-13T13:00:00-04:00">September 13, 1941—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 6:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>962. Embassy’s telegram 949, September 11, 7 p.m.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d345-f1"
                    /> Minister for Foreign Affairs states that he is holding conversations with the
                    Ministers of War and Marine regarding forthcoming staff conversations in
                    Washington. In order to decide finally upon officers to be appointed and
                    instructions to them he and his colleagues would appreciate receiving from our
                    Government more definite data than they now have as result of preliminary
                    conversations with Spears<anchor n="12" xml:id="d345-f2"/> and Christian<anchor
                        n="13" xml:id="d345-f3"/> as to subjects to be discussed and form which
                    agreements mentioned first and last paragraph of Department’s telegram 476, July
                    25, 7 p.m., will take. He seems to understand from Espil that some kind of
                    general form agreement has been drawn up: in any event he presumes that our
                    staff conversations and agreements resulting there from, with other countries
                    within framework of continental defense program would probably enable us to give
                    them an idea what form our agreement with them would take. In the meantime I am
                    giving the Minister the Spanish text of the basic agreement (revised)
                    Department’s circular instructions of July 26<anchor n="14" xml:id="d345-f4"/>
                    1st in the thought that this may possibly be the form agreement which he has in
                    mind although this deals primarily with purchase of military and naval equipment
                    under Lease-Lend agreement, of which I understand from Department’s telegram No.
                    617, September 6, 8 p.m.,<anchor n="11" xml:id="d345-f5"/> the Argentine
                    Government does not desire to avail itself.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Armour</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
